//@version=6
// mVWAP × BB basis setup — the operator's VWAP edge. Script version: v26 (2026-10-23).
// Docs: docs/vwap-setup.md — the walkthrough, tuning table, changelog, and the
// steps for shipping a new version (bump the version above, recreate the alert).
// Four setups in one script, so the same two watchlist alerts carry all of them
// (3, the BB breakout, and 4, the VWAP + BB cross, only send from the 30s alert).
// Each setup has its own "… setup on" switch (v21: the reclaim one in "Setup"): off
// = no markers and no alerts from it, and a VWAP line no setup uses isn't drawn.
// 1) RECLAIM: a top gainer pulls back under its month-anchored VWAP while the
// Bollinger basis (SMA 20) curls up beneath it; the trade is the reclaim. Since
// v11 the same rules also run on the year-anchored VWAP, each line with its own
// stages (the operator's SAIQ 2026-10-05: the spike stopped at the year VWAP,
// based under it, reclaimed it and ran). Messages say which line.
//   FORMING  basis 6–10% under mVWAP, rising, gap closing — or, on a fast approach,
//            price ≤10% under mVWAP and ≥3% above a rising basis → open the chart
//   READY    basis ≤6% under mVWAP — or, on a fast approach, price ≤5% under → entry zone
//   GO       price reclaims mVWAP decisively (close ≥2% above it, under it within 5 bars)
//            or the basis crosses above it (rising) — whichever first, within 60 bars of a
//            FORMING/READY, and never on a bar that closes lower than the bar before
// Price must close at or above the BB basis: a setup under the basis is no
// setup, and a close 2% under it ends the setup — the next reclaim is a fresh READY.
// 2) PULLBACK (v10): a fast run stretches price well above a VWAP line — the
// session, month or (v14) year VWAP — and it comes back down to it.
//   PULLBACK  a close back within 5% above the line after a bar high ≥15% above it → be ready
//             (v24 trial, month and year lines: the bar's low within 5% is enough, its close
//             holding at or above the line)
//   BROKEN    a close under the line → the setup is over (the operator's exit)
//   HELD      price runs +10% from the PULLBACK close first
// Each line runs its own setup, and every message carries its touch number (the
// operator rates the first pullback after the first big move highest; our own
// data found the second as good — docs/vwap-setup.md §13.5).
// 3) BB BREAKOUT (v17): on a 1m candle against a 30s Bollinger Band (20, 2).
//   TOUCH      the forming 1m candle reaches the upper band by its half-minute → get ready
//   BREAKOUT   the 1m candle closes above the band (the close before it didn't) → buy stop over its high
//   TRIGGERED  the next 1m candle trades over that high
// It sends from the 30s alert only: the 30s chart has the 30s band natively, and the
// 1m candles are built from its bars. v18 also draws it on a 1m chart, from the
// 30s bars inside each candle.
// 4) VWAP + BB CROSS (v21): one candle of a timeframe you pick (5m, 1h, …) crosses
// over both a VWAP line — session, and (v22) month or year — and the upper Bollinger
// Band of another timeframe you pick (2m, 30m, 45m, …). Each line runs its own setup.
//   CROSS      the candle opened under both lines (or sitting on the lower one) and a
//              30s close inside it is above both → the alert, while the candle is open
//   LEVEL      (v25) the VB candle closed: its high is the trigger, its low the stop → place a buy stop
//   BREAK      (v25) price reaches that high (when the buy stop fills) → the alert
//              (v26: the level lasts until a candle closes back under the line it crossed)
// Built from the 30s alert's bars, like the breakout; drawn on the candle's own chart.
// Run it as TradingView watchlist alerts — one on 1m and one on 30s (Premium allows 2):
// Symbols = the runners list (dashboard → 📐 sidebar ⋯ → Copy list), session Extended,
// condition = this script → "Any alert() function call", once per bar close,
// webhook = https://pnldash.uz/api/tv/webhook?key=<TV_WEBHOOK_SECRET>.
// The alert message format below is parsed by apps/api/src/services/tv-setups.ts —
// keep the two in step. The offline replica (apps/api/scripts/research/vwap-setup/)
// mirrors this logic; update it with the script.
indicator("mVWAP x BB basis setup", shorttitle = "mVWAP-BB", overlay = true)

// Gainer filter: computed per ticker from its own bars — no screener, no ranking.
// A ticker that doesn't pass stays silent; -100 switches the filter off.
minDayGain = input.float(20.0, "Up at least % (day high vs prior close; -100 = filter off)", group = "Gainer filter (this ticker's own move)")
runnerDays = input.int(3,      "…today, or on any of the last N sessions (0 = today only)", minval = 0, maxval = 5, group = "Gainer filter (this ticker's own move)")
useAhGain  = input.bool(true,  "After hours, also count the move since today's close", group = "Gainer filter (this ticker's own move)")
rcLines    = input.string("Month + Year", "Lines: month VWAP, year VWAP or both (v11)", options = ["Month + Year", "Month", "Year"], group = "Setup")
maxPxBelow = input.float(15.0, "Price at most % under mVWAP", group = "Setup")
formBasis  = input.float(10.0, "FORMING: basis at most % under mVWAP", group = "Setup")
readyBasis = input.float(6.0,  "READY: basis at most % under mVWAP", group = "Setup")
holdTol    = input.float(0.0,  "Price may sit up to % under the basis (0 = must close above it)", group = "Setup")
failPct    = input.float(2.0,  "Setup breaks: close % under the basis", group = "Setup")
slopeBars  = input.int(3,      "Basis rising over N bars", minval = 1, group = "Setup")
useFast    = input.bool(true,  "Fast approach: price leads, the basis lags", group = "Fast approach")
fastAbove  = input.float(3.0,  "Price at least % above the basis", group = "Fast approach")
formPx     = input.float(10.0, "FORMING: price at most % under mVWAP", group = "Fast approach")
readyPx    = input.float(5.0,  "READY: price at most % under mVWAP", group = "Fast approach")
maxBasis   = input.float(15.0, "Basis at most % under mVWAP", group = "Fast approach")
fromBelow  = input.int(10,     "Price under mVWAP for the previous N bars (0 = off)", minval = 0, group = "Fast approach")
maxCycles  = input.int(6,      "Max setups per ticker per day", minval = 1, group = "Alerts")
goMemory   = input.int(60,     "GO up to N bars after the last FORMING/READY (0 = only while armed)", minval = 0, group = "Alerts")
goOn       = input.string("Either", "GO when", options = ["Either", "Price reclaim", "Basis cross"], group = "GO")
goAbovePct = input.float(2.0,  "Price reclaim: close at least % above mVWAP", group = "GO")
goWithin   = input.int(5,      "…having been at/under it within the previous N bars", minval = 1, group = "GO")
alertWin   = input.session("0400-2000", "Alert window (New York time)", group = "Alerts")
pbOn       = input.bool(true,   "Pullback setup on", group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
pbSession  = input.bool(true,   "Lines: session VWAP", inline = "pbl", group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
pbMonth    = input.bool(true,   "month VWAP", inline = "pbl", group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
pbYear     = input.bool(true,   "year VWAP (v14)", inline = "pbl", group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
pbArm      = input.float(15.0,  "Armed: a bar high at least % above the line (the big move)", group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
pbNear     = input.float(5.0,   "PULLBACK: a close back within % above the line", group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
pbBreak    = input.float(0.0,   "BROKEN: a close at least % under the line (0 = any close under it)", group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
pbWin      = input.float(10.0,  "HELD: price runs % above the PULLBACK close", group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
pbMax      = input.int(0,       "Script cap: stop a line after N failed pullbacks a day (0 = none; the dashboard applies the cap since v16)", minval = 0, group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
pbCapMark  = input.int(2,       "Chart: pullbacks after N failed ones are drawn gray (the dashboard's cap)", minval = 1, group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
pbTimeout  = input.int(60,      "Stop watching a pullback after N bars", minval = 1, group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
boOn       = input.bool(true,         "Breakout setup on", group = "BB breakout (v17)")
boBandTf   = input.timeframe("30S",   "BO: BB timeframe (the band; the chart's own, or read from a 1m chart — v18)", group = "BB breakout (v17)")
boTf       = input.timeframe("30S",   "BO: alerts from the alert on this chart timeframe (30S = soonest; 1 = at the 1m close)", group = "BB breakout (v17)")
boLen      = input.int(20,            "BO: BB length", minval = 2, group = "BB breakout (v17)")
boMult     = input.float(2.0,         "BO: BB StdDev", minval = 0.1, group = "BB breakout (v17)")
boMinGain  = input.float(20.0,        "Today's gainers: day high at least % (-100 = filter off)", group = "BB breakout (v17)")
boTouchOn  = input.bool(true,         "TOUCH: the forming 1m candle reaches the band", group = "BB breakout (v17)")
boShow     = input.bool(true,         "Draw the band and markers (on the band's own chart, or a 1m chart — v18)", group = "BB breakout (v17)")
boStrSlope = input.float(0.0,         "Strong: the band up at least % over the last 5 candles (v19; weak = gray)", group = "BB breakout (v17)")
boStrOff   = input.float(10.0,        "Strong: the close at most % under the day's high (v19)", group = "BB breakout (v17)")
boEarlyOn  = input.bool(true,         "Early BO (v20): the first candle to reach +N% today, regular hours, closing above the band", group = "BB breakout (v17)")
boEarlyGain = input.float(10.0,       "Early BO: +N% (day high vs the prior close)", group = "BB breakout (v17)")
boEarlyVol = input.float(2.0,         "Early BO: candle volume at least N× its last 20 candles", minval = 0, group = "BB breakout (v17)")
// v21 inputs go last: TradingView keeps a script's saved input values by position,
// so an input inserted higher up would hand its slot's old value to the wrong input.
rcOn       = input.bool(true,         "Reclaim setup on (FORMING / READY / GO; v21)", group = "Setup")
vbOn       = input.bool(true,         "VWAP + BB cross setup on (v21)", group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbCandleTf = input.timeframe("5",     "VB: candle timeframe — the chart you trade (its candles and session VWAP)", group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbBbTf     = input.timeframe("2",     "VB: BB timeframe (the band)", group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbLen      = input.int(20,            "VB: BB length", minval = 2, group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbMult     = input.float(2.0,         "VB: BB StdDev", minval = 0.1, group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbTol      = input.float(2.0,         "VB: the candle may open up to % above the lower line (price sitting on VWAP; 0 = under both)", minval = 0, group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbGainOn   = input.bool(true,         "VB: gainers only (the gainer filter at the top)", group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbTf       = input.timeframe("30S",   "VB: alerts from the alert on this chart timeframe (30S = soonest)", group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbShow     = input.bool(true,         "VB: draw the band and markers (on the candle timeframe's chart)", group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbSession  = input.bool(true,         "VB lines: session VWAP", inline = "vbl", group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbMonth    = input.bool(true,         "month VWAP (v22)", inline = "vbl", group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbYear     = input.bool(true,         "year VWAP (v22)", inline = "vbl", group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
pbLowMY    = input.bool(true,         "Month / year lines: a candle's low reaching the band counts, its close holding above the line (v24 trial)", group = "Pullback to VWAP (v10)")
vbBreakOn  = input.bool(true,         "VB break (v25): the latest VB candle's high is the trigger — LEVEL when it closes, BREAK when price reaches it", group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")
vbBrkCancel = input.bool(true,        "VB break: a candle closing back under the VWAP line the VB candle crossed cancels the level (v26: the candle's close, not a 30s close)", group = "VWAP + BB cross (v21)")

// Same lines as the chart: VWAP anchor Month on hlc3, BB basis = SMA 20 of close,
// and (v10, PULLBACK) VWAP anchor Session, which resets at timeframe.change("D"),
// the 04:00 ET pre-market open on an Extended chart. Each restarts on the first
// loaded bar too, exactly like TradingView's built-in VWAP
// (`if na(src[1]) … isNewPeriod := true`), so a line never goes blank when its
// anchor isn't in the loaded history (the month line late in a month on 30s).
firstBar = na(hlc3[1])
mvwap  = ta.vwap(hlc3, timeframe.change("M") or firstBar)
svwap  = ta.vwap(hlc3, timeframe.change("D") or firstBar)

// The year line (v11; v14 builds it from hourly bars). An intraday chart loads
// weeks of history, not a year, so a year VWAP from the chart's own bars started
// wherever the history began and differed by timeframe: SDEV 2026-10-05 was 4.36
// on the 30s chart and 4.70 on the 2m alert. v14 takes this year's 60-minute bars
// (extended hours) up to the end of yesterday, from a request that reaches back
// to January, and adds today's bars from the chart, so the 30s chart, the 1m alert
// and the 30s alert share one line. `yearBefore` returns the sums up to the start
// of the current day; they don't depend on the current hour, which is why
// lookahead_on is safe here.
yearBefore() =>
    var float pv    = 0.0
    var float v     = 0.0
    var float pvDay = 0.0
    var float vDay  = 0.0
    if timeframe.change("D")
        pvDay := pv
        vDay  := v
    if timeframe.change("12M")
        pv    := 0.0
        v     := 0.0
        pvDay := 0.0
        vDay  := 0.0
    pv := pv + hlc3 * volume
    v  := v + volume
    [pvDay, vDay]
[yPrevPV, yPrevV] = request.security(ticker.new(syminfo.prefix, syminfo.ticker, session.extended), "60", yearBefore(), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
var float yDayPV = 0.0
var float yDayV  = 0.0
if timeframe.change("D")
    yDayPV := 0.0
    yDayV  := 0.0
yDayPV := yDayPV + hlc3 * volume
yDayV  := yDayV + volume
yvwap = na(yPrevV) or yPrevV + yDayV <= 0 ? na : (yPrevPV + yDayPV) / (yPrevV + yDayV)
basis  = ta.sma(close, 20)
// Strength inputs sent with every signal (v9): the signal bar's volume vs the
// average of the previous 20 bars, and the run-up over the previous 10 bars.
// The server scores GOs with them (services/tv-setups.ts goStrength).
volAvg20 = ta.sma(volume, 20)[1]
volX     = volAvg20 > 0 ? volume / volAvg20 : na
runUp10  = (close / close[10] - 1) * 100
// v21: a line is drawn while a setup that uses it is on.
plot(rcOn or (pbOn and pbMonth) or (vbOn and vbMonth) ? mvwap : na, "mVWAP", color.yellow)
plot(rcOn ? basis : na, "BB basis", color.green)
plot((pbOn and pbSession) or (vbOn and vbSession) ? svwap : na, "sVWAP", color.purple)
plot(rcOn or (pbOn and pbYear) or (vbOn and vbYear) ? yvwap : na, "yVWAP", color.blue)

// Top gainer: today's high vs the prior regular-session close (like Finviz
// Change), or the same in any of the last `runnerDays` sessions — a second- or
// third-day runner sets up BEFORE it is up on the day (MEDS 2026-09-18) — or,
// after hours, the high since today's close (Finviz's AH change: AMOD fell 24%
// on 2026-10-01, then ran +70% after hours from a +19.8% day high).
newDay = timeframe.change("D")
var float lastRegClose = na
var float prevDayClose = na
var float dayHigh      = na
var dayGains = array.new<float>()   // day-high gains of finished sessions, newest first (max 5)
var float ahHigh       = na   // high since today's close (post-market bars)
if newDay
    array.unshift(dayGains, (dayHigh / prevDayClose - 1) * 100)
    if array.size(dayGains) > 5
        array.pop(dayGains)
    prevDayClose := lastRegClose
    dayHigh      := high
    ahHigh       := na
else
    dayHigh := na(dayHigh) ? high : math.max(dayHigh, high)
if session.ismarket
    lastRegClose := close
if session.ispostmarket
    ahHigh := na(ahHigh) ? high : math.max(ahHigh, high)
ahGain = session.ispostmarket and not na(ahHigh) ? (ahHigh / lastRegClose - 1) * 100 : na
dayHighGain = (dayHigh / prevDayClose - 1) * 100
float recentGain = -100.0
lookback = math.min(runnerDays, array.size(dayGains))
if lookback > 0
    for i = 0 to lookback - 1
        g = array.get(dayGains, i)
        if not na(g)
            recentGain := math.max(recentGain, g)
gainer = (not na(dayHighGain) and dayHighGain >= minDayGain) or recentGain >= minDayGain or
     (useAhGain and not na(ahGain) and ahGain >= minDayGain)

// Line-independent parts of the reclaim setup.
basisUp  = basis > basis[slopeBars]
holding  = close >= basis * (1 - holdTol / 100)
inWindow = not na(time(timeframe.period, alertWin, "America/New_York"))

// The reclaim conditions on one line. v11 runs the same rules on the month VWAP
// and the year VWAP. The function is called for each line on every bar, so the
// history inside it (gap closing, the recent-close counts, the cross) stays intact:
// v6 evaluates and/or lazily, and a skipped math.sum would corrupt its history.
// Distances are positive under the line.
// Two shapes. BASE: price consolidates under the line until the basis converges
// (AIXI, VEEA). FAST: price runs at the line while the 20-bar basis lags far
// behind (MEDS 09-18, NIVF 09-30), reached by price distance instead. FAST only
// counts when approaching from below: a spike that falls back to the line (AMOD
// 2026-09-01) is not an approach.
// GO: the basis cross alone fires late on fast moves, because the 20-bar basis
// lags; it crossed near the top on NIVF 2026-09-30 (+40% after the break). The
// decisive price reclaim marks the breakout itself. A cross only counts with the
// basis RISING, and no GO prints on a falling bar: early in a month the line is
// built on thin volume, and one heavy red bar can drag it under a flat basis — a
// "cross" with price below both (AIXI 2026-10-01 09:38).
reclaimConds(float ln) =>
    float pxB    = (ln - close) / ln * 100
    float bB     = (ln - basis) / ln * 100
    bool  gapC   = bB < bB[slopeBars]
    float aboveR = math.sum(close >= ln ? 1.0 : 0.0, math.max(fromBelow, 1))[1]   // closes at/above it, previous `fromBelow` bars
    float underR = math.sum(close <= ln ? 1.0 : 0.0, goWithin)[1]
    bool  crossUp = ta.crossover(basis, ln)
    bool  okLine = gainer and not na(ln) and not na(basis)
    bool  inZ    = okLine and pxB > 0 and pxB <= maxPxBelow and basisUp and holding
    bool  fromOk = fromBelow == 0 or aboveR == 0
    bool  fastA  = useFast and fromOk and close >= basis * (1 + fastAbove / 100) and bB <= maxBasis
    bool  bForm  = bB > readyBasis and bB <= formBasis
    bool  bReady = bB > 0 and bB <= readyBasis
    bool  frm    = inZ and gapC and (bForm or (fastA and pxB <= formPx))
    bool  rdy    = inZ and (bReady or (fastA and pxB <= readyPx))
    bool  recl   = basisUp and underR > 0 and close > ln * (1 + goAbovePct / 100)
    bool  crOk   = crossUp and basisUp
    bool  trig   = goOn == "Basis cross" ? crOk : goOn == "Price reclaim" ? recl : (crOk or recl)
    bool  g      = okLine and trig and close >= close[1]
    [frm, rdy, g, bForm, bReady, recl, bB]

[mForm, mReady, mGo, mBaseForm, mBaseReady, mRecl, mBasisBelow] = reclaimConds(mvwap)
[yForm, yReady, yGo, yBaseForm, yBaseReady, yRecl, yBasisBelow] = reclaimConds(yvwap)

// Stages, per line: 0 idle, 1 forming, 2 ready, 3 go; each fires once per setup.
// A setup that breaks (close under the line and failPct under the basis) re-arms.
// GO also fires within `goMemory` bars of the last FORMING/READY when a break
// came in between (AIXI 2026-10-02: READY, dip under the basis, then one bar
// back over both lines). Outside the alert window nothing fires and no stage advances.
type RcLine
    int stage        = 0
    int cycles       = 0
    int lastSetupBar = na

// One bar of one line's stage machine; returns the stage that fires (0 = none).
method advance(RcLine s, float ln, bool frm, bool rdy, bool g) =>
    if s.stage > 0 and close < ln and close < basis * (1 - failPct / 100)
        s.stage := 0
    bool recentSetup = goMemory > 0 and not na(s.lastSetupBar) and bar_index - s.lastSetupBar <= goMemory
    int target = 0
    if g and s.stage < 3 and (s.stage >= 1 or recentSetup)
        target := 3
    else if rdy
        target := 2
    else if frm
        target := 1
    bool fire = inWindow and target > s.stage and (s.stage > 0 or target == 3 or s.cycles < maxCycles)
    if fire
        if s.stage == 0 and target < 3
            s.cycles := s.cycles + 1
        if target < 3
            s.lastSetupBar := bar_index
        s.stage := target
    fire ? target : 0

var RcLine rcM = RcLine.new()
var RcLine rcY = RcLine.new()
if newDay
    rcM.stage        := 0
    rcM.cycles       := 0
    rcM.lastSetupBar := na
    rcY.stage        := 0
    rcY.cycles       := 0
    rcY.lastSetupBar := na
int fireM = 0
int fireY = 0
if rcOn and rcLines != "Year"
    fireM := rcM.advance(mvwap, mForm, mReady, mGo)
if rcOn and rcLines != "Month"
    fireY := rcY.advance(yvwap, yForm, yReady, yGo)

pctVs(float ln) => (close >= ln ? "+" : "") + str.tostring((close / ln - 1) * 100, "#.0")
// The message is a contract with services/tv-setups.ts parseTvMessage. `basis %`
// is measured against the setup's own line:
//   READY AIXI 1.48 | mVWAP 1.57 (-5.7%) | yVWAP 2.9 (-49.0%) | basis 1.49 (-5.1%) | line month | day high +41% | vol 1.2x | run +3.0% | tf 1 | path base
rcMsg(int target, string lineName, float bBelow, bool bForm, bool bReady, bool recl) =>
    string msg = (target == 3 ? "GO" : target == 2 ? "READY" : "FORMING") + " " + syminfo.ticker + " " + str.tostring(close, format.mintick)
    msg += " | mVWAP " + str.tostring(mvwap, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(mvwap) + "%)"
    if not na(yvwap)
        msg += " | yVWAP " + str.tostring(yvwap, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(yvwap) + "%)"
    msg += " | basis " + str.tostring(basis, format.mintick) + " (" + str.tostring(-bBelow, "#.0") + "%)"
    msg += " | line " + lineName
    msg += " | day high " + (dayHighGain >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(dayHighGain, "#") + "%"
    if not na(ahGain)
        msg += " | ah " + (ahGain >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(ahGain, "#") + "%"
    if not na(volX)
        msg += " | vol " + str.tostring(volX, "#.#") + "x"
    if not na(runUp10)
        msg += " | run " + (runUp10 >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(runUp10, "#.#") + "%"
    msg += " | tf " + timeframe.period
    if target < 3
        msg += " | path " + ((target == 2 ? bReady : bForm) ? "base" : "fast")
    else
        msg += " | via " + (recl and goOn != "Basis cross" ? "reclaim" : "cross")
    msg

// Both lines firing the same stage on one bar (they can sit close together) is
// one "line month+year" message (v11–v13 said "both"), with the month line's
// basis distance.
if fireM > 0 and fireM == fireY
    alert(rcMsg(fireM, "month+year", mBasisBelow, mBaseForm, mBaseReady, mRecl), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
else
    if fireM > 0
        alert(rcMsg(fireM, "month", mBasisBelow, mBaseForm, mBaseReady, mRecl), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
    if fireY > 0
        alert(rcMsg(fireY, "year", yBasisBelow, yBaseForm, yBaseReady, yRecl), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

// ── 2) PULLBACK (v10) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// A fast run stretches price well above a VWAP line and it comes back down to it
// (operator, 2026-10-05: SAIQ and SDEV on the session line, VEEA 2026-09-15 on
// the month line, MI 2026-10-05 12:40 ET on the year line). Each line keeps its
// own state, reset every day:
//   armed     by a bar high ≥ pbArm% above the line (gainers only)
//   PULLBACK  on a LATER close within pbNear% above the line ("be ready")
//   BROKEN    then a close pbBreak% under the line — the operator's exit — or
//   HELD      a high +pbWin% above the PULLBACK close, whichever comes first;
//             after pbTimeout bars the pullback is dropped silently.
// A close straight through the line while armed is a touch with no PULLBACK.
// Re-arming needs a new bar high ≥ pbArm% above the line. v15: the day's cap
// (pbMax) counts FAILED pullbacks — BROKEN or straight through — not every touch.
// A line that keeps holding keeps alerting (MI 2026-10-05: six year-line touches,
// every alerted one HELD, but v14's 2-touch cap blocked 11:44, 12:37 and 12:57);
// a line that failed twice stops. Four months of session-line data: at least as good
// on every exit rule, ~2 more alerts a day (docs/vwap-setup.md §13.5).
// v16 (2026-10-10): the cap moved to the dashboard. The script alerts every
// pullback (pbMax 0) and each PULLBACK says how many failed before it on its line
// (`fails N`); the server stays quiet past 2 failures unless the ticker is on our
// Momentum list at grade B+ or better (WFF 10-09: a year-line pullback ran +40%
// past the cap). Cap tweaks no longer need a new script or new alerts.
type PbLine
    bool  armed    = false
    int   armBar   = na
    float peakPct  = na
    int   touches  = 0
    int   fails    = 0
    bool  open     = false
    float entry    = na
    int   alertBar = na

// One bar of one line's setup: 0 nothing, 1 PULLBACK, 2 BROKEN, 3 HELD.
// v24 (operator, RBNE 10-21 04:10 ET: the dip tagged the month line's band with its
// low, ~1.20 over a ~1.17 line, but closed 7–8% above it, then ran to 1.92): `useLow`
// lets the bar's low reach the band, the close still at or above the line. A trial on
// the month and year lines only — on four months of the session line (research/
// vwap-pullback --touch low) the low added ~2 alerts a day at 0.3–0.9 points worse a
// trade, and the month and year lines can only be graded live. Such a PULLBACK's
// message shows its close more than pbNear % above the line.
method step(PbLine s, float ln, bool canArm, bool useLow) =>
    int ev = 0
    if not na(ln) and ln > 0
        if s.open
            if close < ln * (1 - pbBreak / 100)
                s.open  := false
                s.fails := s.fails + 1
                ev := 2
            else if high >= s.entry * (1 + pbWin / 100)
                s.open := false
                ev := 3
            else if bar_index - s.alertBar >= pbTimeout
                s.open := false
        if not s.open
            float stretch = (high / ln - 1) * 100
            if not s.armed
                if canArm and stretch >= pbArm
                    s.armed   := true
                    s.armBar  := bar_index
                    s.peakPct := stretch
            else
                s.peakPct := math.max(s.peakPct, stretch)
                float reach = useLow ? low : close
                if bar_index > s.armBar and reach <= ln * (1 + pbNear / 100)
                    s.armed   := false
                    s.touches := s.touches + 1
                    if close < ln * (1 - pbBreak / 100)
                        s.fails := s.fails + 1
                    else if ev == 0 and (pbMax == 0 or s.fails < pbMax)
                        s.open     := true
                        s.entry    := close
                        s.alertBar := bar_index
                        ev := 1
    ev

var PbLine pbS = PbLine.new()
var PbLine pbM = PbLine.new()
var PbLine pbY = PbLine.new()
if newDay
    pbS.armed   := false
    pbS.open    := false
    pbS.touches := 0
    pbS.fails   := 0
    pbM.armed   := false
    pbM.open    := false
    pbM.touches := 0
    pbM.fails   := 0
    pbY.armed   := false
    pbY.open    := false
    pbY.touches := 0
    pbY.fails   := 0
int evS = 0
int evM = 0
int evY = 0
if pbOn and inWindow
    if pbSession
        evS := pbS.step(svwap, gainer, false)
    if pbMonth
        evM := pbM.step(mvwap, gainer, pbLowMY)
    if pbYear
        evY := pbY.step(yvwap, gainer, pbLowMY)

// The message — a contract with services/tv-setups.ts parseTvMessage, like the RECLAIM one:
//   PULLBACK SAIQ 6.2 | sVWAP 6.16 (+0.7%) | mVWAP 4.1 (+51.2%) | line session | touch 2 | fails 0 | peak +17% | day high +336% | vol 0.6x | run -9.6% | tf 1
// v16: `fails` = failed pullbacks on the line before this one (the lowest of the lines named).
pbMsg(int ev, string lineName, int touch, float peak, int fails) =>
    string msg = (ev == 1 ? "PULLBACK" : ev == 2 ? "BROKEN" : "HELD") + " " + syminfo.ticker + " " + str.tostring(close, format.mintick)
    msg += " | sVWAP " + str.tostring(svwap, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(svwap) + "%)"
    msg += " | mVWAP " + str.tostring(mvwap, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(mvwap) + "%)"
    if not na(yvwap)
        msg += " | yVWAP " + str.tostring(yvwap, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(yvwap) + "%)"
    msg += " | line " + lineName + " | touch " + str.tostring(touch)
    if ev == 1
        msg += " | fails " + str.tostring(fails)
    if ev == 1 and not na(peak)
        msg += " | peak +" + str.tostring(peak, "#") + "%"
    msg += " | day high " + (dayHighGain >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(dayHighGain, "#") + "%"
    if not na(ahGain)
        msg += " | ah " + (ahGain >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(ahGain, "#") + "%"
    if not na(volX)
        msg += " | vol " + str.tostring(volX, "#.#") + "x"
    if not na(runUp10)
        msg += " | run " + (runUp10 >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(runUp10, "#.#") + "%"
    msg + " | tf " + timeframe.period

// Lines firing the same event on one bar (they sit close together early in a
// month) are one message naming all of them, e.g. "line session+month" (v10–v13
// said "both" for session + month): the lowest touch number and failure count, the highest peak.
pbJoin(string acc, string name) => acc == "" ? name : acc + "+" + name
pbFire(int e) =>
    string names = ""
    int touch = 999
    int fails = 999
    float peak = na
    if evS == e
        names := pbJoin(names, "session")
        touch := math.min(touch, pbS.touches)
        fails := math.min(fails, pbS.fails)
        peak  := na(peak) ? pbS.peakPct : math.max(peak, nz(pbS.peakPct, peak))
    if evM == e
        names := pbJoin(names, "month")
        touch := math.min(touch, pbM.touches)
        fails := math.min(fails, pbM.fails)
        peak  := na(peak) ? pbM.peakPct : math.max(peak, nz(pbM.peakPct, peak))
    if evY == e
        names := pbJoin(names, "year")
        touch := math.min(touch, pbY.touches)
        fails := math.min(fails, pbY.fails)
        peak  := na(peak) ? pbY.peakPct : math.max(peak, nz(pbY.peakPct, peak))
    [names, touch, peak, fails]

[pbN1, pbT1, pbP1, pbF1] = pbFire(1)
[pbN2, pbT2, pbP2, pbF2] = pbFire(2)
[pbN3, pbT3, pbP3, pbF3] = pbFire(3)
if pbN1 != ""
    alert(pbMsg(1, pbN1, pbT1, pbP1, pbF1), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if pbN2 != ""
    alert(pbMsg(2, pbN2, pbT2, pbP2, pbF2), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if pbN3 != ""
    alert(pbMsg(3, pbN3, pbT3, pbP3, pbF3), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

// v16: a pullback past the dashboard's cap (pbCapMark failures on every line it names)
// is drawn gray — it only pings for a B+-or-better ticker on our Momentum list.
bool pbCapped = pbN1 != "" and pbF1 >= pbCapMark
plotshape(pbN1 != "" and not pbCapped, "Pullback", shape.diamond, location.belowbar, color.aqua, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(pbCapped, "Pullback (past the cap)", shape.diamond, location.belowbar, color.gray, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(evS == 2 or evM == 2 or evY == 2, "Broken", shape.xcross, location.abovebar, color.red, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(evS == 3 or evM == 3 or evY == 3, "Held", shape.flag, location.abovebar, color.lime, size = size.tiny)
// Reclaim markers: the month line orange / yellow / green as before, the year line
// (v13) the same shapes in blue like its line. A stage that fires on both lines on
// one bar shows the month marker.
plotshape(fireM == 1, "Forming (month)", shape.circle, location.belowbar, color.orange, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(fireM == 2, "Ready (month)", shape.triangleup, location.belowbar, color.yellow, size = size.small)
plotshape(fireM == 3, "Go (month)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.lime, text = "GO", textcolor = color.black, size = size.small)
plotshape(fireY == 1 and fireM != 1, "Forming (year)", shape.circle, location.belowbar, color.blue, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(fireY == 2 and fireM != 2, "Ready (year)", shape.triangleup, location.belowbar, color.blue, size = size.small)
plotshape(fireY == 3 and fireM != 3, "Go (year)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.blue, text = "GO", textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)
alertcondition(fireM == 2 or fireY == 2, "READY", "READY {{ticker}} {{close}} | tf {{interval}}")
alertcondition(fireM == 3 or fireY == 3, "GO", "GO {{ticker}} {{close}} | tf {{interval}}")

// ── 3) BB BREAKOUT (v17; v18 draws it on a 1m chart too) ──────────────────────
// The operator's third setup (2026-10-18; NWGL, HODO, XLAB, SGRX, XXII on 10-15/16):
// a 1m chart with the Bollinger Band computed on 30s bars ("the 1m upper band
// crosses the 1m chart too often"). A 1m candle closes above the upper band and
// the next candle takes out its high. Measured on 20 sessions of +20% names
// (research/bb-breakout): about break-even on its own, so the dashboard stores
// and grades every signal and pings none (a trial).
//   TOUCH      the forming candle's high reaches the band before the minute closes
//              (on 30s bars: at the half-minute), the last 1m close was under it
//   BREAKOUT   the 1m candle closes above the band, the close before it didn't;
//              the trade is a buy stop one tick over its high, the stop its low
//   TRIGGERED  a bar of the next 1m candle trades at or over that trigger
//              (seen at the 30s bar's close); the candle passing without it ends it
// Candles are clock minutes; a minute with no trades has no candle. Two ways to
// see the band (`boBandTf`, 30S):
//   on its own chart (30s): the chart's BB, 1m candles built from its bars;
//   on a 1m chart (v18): the 30s bars inside each candle (request.security_lower_tf),
//   so TOUCH is any 30s bar before the last reaching the band, and a TOUCH and a
//   BREAKOUT can land on one 1m bar (the chart then shows the BREAKOUT).
// Same rules either way. Alerts go out only from the chart timeframe `boTf` (the
// 30s alert: a TOUCH comes 30 s before the candle closes; from the 1m alert it
// would arrive with the BREAKOUT). Other chart timeframes draw nothing.
// v19 (operator: "some BOs are not very accurate maybe? 18:14, 18:44, 19:30" on
// XLAB 10-16): each signal says how the band moved over the last 5 candles
// (`slope`) and how far the close is under the day's high (`off high`). Strong =
// the band not falling and the close within 10% of the high; weak ones are drawn
// gray and the dashboard dims them. On 20 sessions (research/bb-breakout) strong
// breakouts did +0.41% a trade and weak ones -0.17%, the same in both halves;
// a bounce into a band still falling from the top (XLAB 19:30) is the weak kind.
// v20 (operator, 10-19, after WORX ran 1.40 → 2.54 with no BO — its first break came
// at +9%, and by +20% it was riding the band, never a fresh cross): an EARLY BO on
// the first candle of the day to reach +10% (day high vs the prior close), in regular
// hours, closing above the band, on at least 2× its last 20 candles' volume — no
// +20% filter, no fresh-cross test. Measured on every night-before watchlist name
// (research/bb-breakout/early_study.py): +0.29% a trade, ~8 a day, both halves;
// the same rule before or after regular hours lost (-2.7% / -3.2%), and without the
// volume test it was +0.14%. A trial: the message says `early +10%`, the chart
// draws an orange "E", and its TRIGGERED doesn't need the +20% filter either.
boChartSec = timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period)
boBandSec  = timeframe.in_seconds(boBandTf)
boNative   = boChartSec == boBandSec and boChartSec <= 60
boFrom1m   = boChartSec == 60 and boBandSec < 60
boValid    = boOn and (boNative or boFrom1m)
boSend     = boValid and timeframe.period == boTf
boBasis    = ta.sma(close, boLen)
boUpper    = boBasis + boMult * ta.stdev(close, boLen)
// The band on the 30s bars inside a 1m bar, and their highs. Requested on every
// chart (a request can't be conditional); off a 1m chart, or on one that neither
// draws nor sends the breakout (the 1m watchlist alert created with "Draw" off),
// it asks for the chart's own timeframe, which is one cheap value per bar.
boUse1m = boFrom1m and (boShow or boSend)
boBand() =>
    float b = ta.sma(close, boLen)
    [b + boMult * ta.stdev(close, boLen), high]
[boInUp, boInHigh] = request.security_lower_tf(syminfo.tickerid, boUse1m ? boBandTf : timeframe.period, boBand())
int   boInN = array.size(boInUp)
float boUp  = boNative ? boUpper : boUse1m and boInN > 0 ? array.get(boInUp, boInN - 1) : na   // the band at this bar's close
boGainer = boMinGain <= -100 or (not na(dayHighGain) and dayHighGain >= boMinGain) or
     (useAhGain and not na(ahGain) and ahGain >= boMinGain)

var int   boMin     = na      // the clock minute (ms) the forming 1m candle started
var float boCHigh   = na
var float boCLow    = na
var float boCVol    = 0.0
var bool  boTouched = false
var float boPrevC   = na      // the last finished 1m candle's close…
var float boPrevU   = na      // …and the band at that close
var int   boArmMin  = na      // an armed BREAKOUT: the minute its trigger candle starts
var float boTrig    = na
var float boStop    = na
var float boVolX    = na
var boVols = array.new<float>()   // the last 20 finished candles' volumes
var boLows = array.new<float>()   // the last 30 finished candles' lows
var bool  boDone    = true    // the forming candle has closed
var float boLastC   = na      // the forming candle's latest close and band, to close it
var float boLastU   = na      // if its closing 30s bar has no trades (and so no bar)
var boUps = array.new<float>()    // the band at the close of the last 5 finished candles (v19)
var float boArmSlope  = na        // the armed BREAKOUT's context, repeated on its TRIGGERED
var float boArmOff    = na
var bool  boArmStrong = false
var bool  boEarlyDone = false     // v20: today's first +boEarlyGain% candle has passed
var bool  boArmEarly  = false     // the armed BREAKOUT is an early one
if newDay
    boEarlyDone := false

int boMinNow = time - time % 60000
if na(boMin) or boMinNow != boMin
    if not boDone and not na(boLastC)
        // The last candle's closing 30s bar had no trades: close it on its last bar
        // (no BREAKOUT for it, but the next candle's "fresh" test stays right).
        boPrevC := boLastC
        boPrevU := boLastU
        array.push(boVols, boCVol)
        if array.size(boVols) > 20
            array.shift(boVols)
        array.push(boLows, boCLow)
        if array.size(boLows) > 30
            array.shift(boLows)
        array.push(boUps, boLastU)
        if array.size(boUps) > 5
            array.shift(boUps)
    if not na(boArmMin) and boMinNow > boArmMin
        boArmMin := na                         // the trigger candle passed (or had no trades)
    boDone    := false
    boMin     := boMinNow
    boCHigh   := high
    boCLow    := low
    boCVol    := volume
    boTouched := false
else
    boCHigh := math.max(boCHigh, high)
    boCLow  := math.min(boCLow, low)
    boCVol  := boCVol + volume
bool boEnds  = time_close % 60000 == 0           // this bar closes the 1m candle (every bar of a 1m chart)
bool boFresh = not na(boPrevC) and not na(boPrevU) and boPrevC <= boPrevU
float boLow30 = array.size(boLows) > 0 ? math.min(array.min(boLows), boCLow) : boCLow
float boRun30 = (close / boLow30 - 1) * 100      // the run over the last 30 minutes

// TOUCH on a 1m chart: a 30s bar before the candle's last whose candle high so far reaches its band.
bool boInTouch = false
if boUse1m and boInN > 1
    float runHi = na
    for k = 0 to boInN - 2
        runHi := na(runHi) ? array.get(boInHigh, k) : math.max(runHi, array.get(boInHigh, k))
        float uk = array.get(boInUp, k)
        if not boInTouch and not na(uk) and runHi >= uk
            boInTouch := true

boLastC := close
boLastU := boUp
// v19 context: the band now vs at the close 5 candles ago, and the close vs the day's high so far.
float boSlope  = array.size(boUps) >= 5 and array.get(boUps, 0) > 0 ? (boUp / array.get(boUps, 0) - 1) * 100 : na
float boOff    = not na(dayHigh) and dayHigh > 0 ? (close / dayHigh - 1) * 100 : na
bool  boStrong = not na(boSlope) and boSlope >= boStrSlope and not na(boOff) and boOff >= -boStrOff
bool boCalc    = boValid and inWindow and boGainer and not na(boUp)
bool boTrigEv  = false
bool boTouchEv = false
bool boBreakEv = false
bool boEarlyEv = false
if not na(boArmMin) and boMin == boArmMin and high >= boTrig
    boArmMin := na
    boTrigEv := boArmEarly ? boValid and inWindow and not na(boUp) : boCalc
if boCalc and boTouchOn and not boTouched and boFresh and (boNative ? not boEnds and boCHigh >= boUp : boInTouch)
    boTouched := true
    boTouchEv := true
if boEnds
    boVolX := array.size(boVols) > 0 and array.avg(boVols) > 0 ? boCVol / array.avg(boVols) : na
    // v20 early: the first candle of the day whose day high reaches +boEarlyGain%.
    bool firstCross = not boEarlyDone and not na(dayHighGain) and dayHighGain >= boEarlyGain
    if firstCross
        boEarlyDone := true
    bool early   = boEarlyOn and firstCross and boValid and inWindow and session.ismarket and not na(boUp) and
         close > boUp and not na(boVolX) and boVolX >= boEarlyVol
    bool regular = boCalc and boFresh and close > boUp
    if early or regular
        boArmMin  := boMin + 60000
        boTrig    := boCHigh + syminfo.mintick
        boStop    := boCLow
        boArmSlope  := boSlope
        boArmOff    := boOff
        boArmStrong := boStrong
        boArmEarly  := early
        boEarlyEv := early
        boBreakEv := true
    boPrevC := close
    boPrevU := boUp
    array.push(boVols, boCVol)
    if array.size(boVols) > 20
        array.shift(boVols)
    array.push(boLows, boCLow)
    if array.size(boLows) > 30
        array.shift(boLows)
    array.push(boUps, boUp)
    if array.size(boUps) > 5
        array.shift(boUps)
    boDone := true

// The message — a contract with services/tv-setups.ts parseTvMessage:
//   TOUCH XLAB 2.29 | upper 2.3 (-0.4%) | sVWAP 2.01 (+13.9%) | day high +80% | run30 +12% | tf 30S
//   BREAKOUT XLAB 2.38 | upper 2.33 (+2.1%) | trigger 2.41 | stop 2.25 | sVWAP 2.01 (+18.4%) | day high +90% | vol 3.2x | run30 +17% | slope +4.1% | off high -1.2% | tf 30S
// v19: `slope` (the band over the last 5 candles) and `off high` (the close vs the day's high);
// a TRIGGERED repeats its BREAKOUT's.
//   TRIGGERED XLAB 2.42 | upper 2.35 (+3.0%) | trigger 2.41 | stop 2.25 | sVWAP 2.02 (+19.8%) | day high +92% | run30 +19% | tf 30S
// v20: an early BO (and its TRIGGERED) adds `early +10%`:
//   BREAKOUT WORX 1.5 | upper 1.44 (+4.2%) | trigger 1.53 | stop 1.39 | sVWAP 1.41 (+6.4%) | day high +10% | vol 6.1x | run30 +9% | early +10% | slope +2.0% | off high -1.3% | tf 30S
boMsg(int ev) =>
    string msg = (ev == 1 ? "TOUCH" : ev == 2 ? "BREAKOUT" : "TRIGGERED") + " " + syminfo.ticker + " " + str.tostring(close, format.mintick)
    msg += " | upper " + str.tostring(boUp, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(boUp) + "%)"
    if ev >= 2
        msg += " | trigger " + str.tostring(boTrig, format.mintick) + " | stop " + str.tostring(boStop, format.mintick)
    if not na(svwap)
        msg += " | sVWAP " + str.tostring(svwap, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(svwap) + "%)"
    if not na(dayHighGain)
        msg += " | day high " + (dayHighGain >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(dayHighGain, "#") + "%"
    if not na(ahGain)
        msg += " | ah " + (ahGain >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(ahGain, "#") + "%"
    if ev == 2 and not na(boVolX)
        msg += " | vol " + str.tostring(boVolX, "#.#") + "x"
    if not na(boRun30)
        msg += " | run30 +" + str.tostring(math.max(boRun30, 0), "#") + "%"
    if (ev == 2 and boEarlyEv) or (ev == 3 and boArmEarly)
        msg += " | early +" + str.tostring(boEarlyGain, "#") + "%"
    float sl  = ev == 3 ? boArmSlope : boSlope
    float offH = ev == 3 ? boArmOff : boOff
    if not na(sl)
        msg += " | slope " + (sl >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(sl, "#.0") + "%"
    if not na(offH)
        msg += " | off high " + str.tostring(offH, "#.0") + "%"
    msg + " | tf " + timeframe.period

if boSend and boTrigEv
    alert(boMsg(3), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if boSend and boTouchEv
    alert(boMsg(1), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if boSend and boBreakEv
    alert(boMsg(2), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
plot(boShow and boValid ? boUp : na, "BB upper (breakout)", color.new(color.fuchsia, 40))
// v19: strong signals fuchsia, weak ones (band falling, or >10% under the day's high) gray.
plotshape(boShow and boTouchEv and not boBreakEv, "BB touch", shape.circle, location.abovebar, boStrong ? color.fuchsia : color.gray, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(boShow and boBreakEv and not boEarlyEv, "Breakout", shape.labeldown, location.abovebar, boStrong ? color.fuchsia : color.gray, text = "BO", textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)
plotshape(boShow and boEarlyEv, "Early breakout (v20)", shape.labeldown, location.abovebar, color.orange, text = "E", textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)
plotshape(boShow and boTrigEv, "Triggered", shape.triangleup, location.belowbar, boArmEarly ? color.orange : boArmStrong ? color.fuchsia : color.gray, size = size.small)

// ── 4) VWAP + BB CROSS (v21; v22 adds the month and year lines) ───────────────
// The operator's fourth setup (2026-10-20; AIXI, WORX and NWGL on 5m charts): "the
// market is colder than before, and it's very hard to trade with 1min timeframe".
// On a chart of their choice (5m, 1h, …) with its session VWAP and the upper
// Bollinger Band of another timeframe (2m on the 5m chart; 30m or 45m on the 1h
// chart), one candle crosses over both lines. They want the alert at that moment,
// not at the candle's close. v22 (operator: "it's ok to add a support for month and
// year"): the same rule on the month and the year VWAP, each line with its own state.
//   CROSS  at a 30s close inside the candle, its open is at or under both the line and
//          the band as they stand then (at most vbTol % over the lower one: price
//          sitting on the line counts) and the close is above both → the alert; once
//          per candle and line. v23 (operator, WHLR 10-21 04:00 ET: "this one
//          definitely should be considered as a VB … if 1 candle crosses both vwap and
//          bb upper row"): the lines as they stand at that close — what the chart
//          draws for the candle — not as they stood when it opened, and the day's
//          first candle counts. A 04:00 gap-and-go (WHLR 0.36 → open 0.43 → 0.55)
//          drags its own VWAP and band above its open; v21/v22 saw an open above
//          yesterday's lines and stayed silent.
// Premium's two watchlist-alert slots are taken (1m + 30s), so it rides the 30s alert
// like the breakout: vbStep() builds the candle, its VWAP lines and the band (SMA /
// StdDev of the BB timeframe's closes, the forming one live) from the 30s bars. The
// session line is the candle timeframe's own (hlc3 × volume of its candles). A 30s
// chart doesn't hold a month of history, so the month and year lines take the days
// before today from this year's hourly bars (vbAnchors(), like the year line since
// v14) and add today's candles. The candle's chart replays the same 30s bars
// (request.security_lower_tf), so its markers are the alerts. Gainers only by
// default: the filter at the top, recomputed from the 30s bars
// (a request can't read the chart's running values). Lines firing on one 30s bar are
// one message (`line session+month`); `cross N` counts the day's crosses on each line
// (the lowest of the lines named), and the server announces the first few
// (TV_SETUP.vb_cap).
vbOk = vbOn and timeframe.in_seconds(vbCandleTf) >= timeframe.in_seconds(vbTf) and timeframe.in_seconds(vbBbTf) >= timeframe.in_seconds(vbTf)

// The month's and the year's Σ hlc3 × volume and Σ volume up to the start of the
// current day, on hourly bars (extended hours). They don't depend on the current
// hour, which is why lookahead_on is safe here (as in yearBefore()).
vbAnchors() =>
    var float aMPV  = 0.0
    var float aMV   = 0.0
    var float aYPV  = 0.0
    var float aYV   = 0.0
    var float aMPVd = 0.0
    var float aMVd  = 0.0
    var float aYPVd = 0.0
    var float aYVd  = 0.0
    bool aNewDay   = timeframe.change("D")
    bool aNewMonth = timeframe.change("M")
    bool aNewYear  = timeframe.change("12M")
    if aNewDay
        aMPVd := aMPV
        aMVd  := aMV
        aYPVd := aYPV
        aYVd  := aYV
    if aNewMonth
        aMPV  := 0.0
        aMV   := 0.0
        aMPVd := 0.0
        aMVd  := 0.0
    if aNewYear
        aYPV  := 0.0
        aYV   := 0.0
        aYPVd := 0.0
        aYVd  := 0.0
    aMPV := aMPV + hlc3 * volume
    aMV  := aMV + volume
    aYPV := aYPV + hlc3 * volume
    aYV  := aYV + volume
    [aMPVd, aMVd, aYPVd, aYVd]

// One line's CROSS test, on the line and the band as they stand now (v23): the candle's
// open is at or under the higher of them and at most vbTol % over the lower one, and
// the close is above both — the candle's body crosses both.
vbCan(float ln, float up, float cOpen, bool fired) =>
    not fired and not na(ln) and not na(up) and cOpen <= math.max(ln, up) and cOpen <= math.min(ln, up) * (1 + vbTol / 100) and close > ln and close > up

// v26: the lowest of the VWAP lines a VB candle crossed (session / month / year), na if none is known.
vbLowest(bool onS, bool onM, bool onY, float lnS, float lnM, float lnY) =>
    float lowLn = na
    if onS and not na(lnS)
        lowLn := lnS
    if onM and not na(lnM)
        lowLn := na(lowLn) ? lnM : math.min(lowLn, lnM)
    if onY and not na(lnY)
        lowLn := na(lowLn) ? lnY : math.min(lowLn, lnY)
    lowLn

vbStep() =>
    // Called on every bar: and/or are lazy in v6, so the timeframe tests and the
    // request come first.
    bool gNewDay   = timeframe.change("D")
    bool vNewBb    = timeframe.change(vbBbTf)
    bool vNewCndl  = timeframe.change(vbCandleTf)
    bool vInWin    = not na(time(timeframe.period, alertWin, "America/New_York"))
    [vMBPV, vMBV, vYBPV, vYBV] = request.security(ticker.new(syminfo.prefix, syminfo.ticker, session.extended), "60", vbAnchors(), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
    // The gainer filter, as at the top of the script.
    var float gLastReg = na
    var float gPrev    = na
    var float gHigh    = na
    var float gAhHigh  = na
    var gGains = array.new<float>()   // finished sessions' day-high gains, newest first (max 5)
    if gNewDay
        array.unshift(gGains, (gHigh / gPrev - 1) * 100)
        if array.size(gGains) > 5
            array.pop(gGains)
        gPrev   := gLastReg
        gHigh   := high
        gAhHigh := na
    else
        gHigh := na(gHigh) ? high : math.max(gHigh, high)
    if session.ismarket
        gLastReg := close
    if session.ispostmarket
        gAhHigh := na(gAhHigh) ? high : math.max(gAhHigh, high)
    float gAh     = session.ispostmarket and not na(gAhHigh) ? (gAhHigh / gLastReg - 1) * 100 : na
    float gDay    = (gHigh / gPrev - 1) * 100
    float gRecent = -100.0
    int   gLook   = math.min(runnerDays, array.size(gGains))
    if gLook > 0
        for i = 0 to gLook - 1
            float gOne = array.get(gGains, i)
            if not na(gOne)
                gRecent := math.max(gRecent, gOne)
    bool gOk = (not na(gDay) and gDay >= minDayGain) or gRecent >= minDayGain or (useAhGain and not na(gAh) and gAh >= minDayGain)
    // The band: the BB timeframe's last vbLen - 1 finished closes plus the forming one.
    var vCloses = array.new<float>()
    var float vLastC = na
    if vNewBb and not na(vLastC)
        array.push(vCloses, vLastC)
        if array.size(vCloses) > vbLen - 1
            array.shift(vCloses)
    vLastC := close
    float vBand = na
    int   vN    = array.size(vCloses)
    if vN == vbLen - 1
        float vSum = close
        for i = 0 to vN - 1
            vSum := vSum + array.get(vCloses, i)
        float vMean = vSum / vbLen
        float vSq   = math.pow(close - vMean, 2)
        for i = 0 to vN - 1
            vSq := vSq + math.pow(array.get(vCloses, i) - vMean, 2)
        vBand := vMean + vbMult * math.sqrt(vSq / vbLen)
    // The candle, and the day's Σ over its finished candles.
    var float vPV      = 0.0     // Σ hlc3 × volume…
    var float vV       = 0.0     // …and Σ volume
    var float vOpen    = na
    var float vHigh    = na
    var float vLow     = na
    var float vClose   = na
    var float vVol     = 0.0
    var bool  vSFired  = false
    var bool  vMFired  = false
    var bool  vYFired  = false
    var int   vSCount  = 0
    var int   vMCount  = 0
    var int   vYCount  = 0
    var vVols = array.new<float>()   // the last 20 finished candles' volumes
    // v25: the latest VB candle's high (the trigger) and low (the stop), and the lines it crossed.
    var float vLvHigh   = na
    var float vLvLow    = na
    var bool  vLvS      = false
    var bool  vLvM      = false
    var bool  vLvY      = false
    var bool  vLvOn     = false
    var int   vBrkCount = 0
    var float vPrevVw   = na     // v26: the last bar's lines (where they stood at the candle's close)
    var float vPrevMw   = na
    var float vPrevYw   = na
    bool vSet = false
    bool vBrk = false
    if gNewDay or vNewCndl or na(vOpen)
        // The candle that just closed (its values are still here): a VB candle sets the level,
        // replacing the last one. A new day clears it.
        if gNewDay
            vLvOn     := false
            vBrkCount := 0
        else if vbBreakOn and not na(vOpen) and (vSFired or vMFired or vYFired)
            vLvHigh := vHigh
            vLvLow  := vLow
            vLvS    := vSFired
            vLvM    := vMFired
            vLvY    := vYFired
            vLvOn   := true
            vSet    := true
        // v26: that candle — the VB candle itself or a later one — closed under the lowest line the
        // VB candle crossed: the level is cancelled (and a level that dies here isn't sent).
        if vbBrkCancel and vLvOn and not na(vOpen)
            float vLnC = vbLowest(vLvS, vLvM, vLvY, vPrevVw, vPrevMw, vPrevYw)
            if not na(vLnC) and vClose < vLnC
                vLvOn := false
                vSet  := false
        if not na(vOpen)
            array.push(vVols, vVol)
            if array.size(vVols) > 20
                array.shift(vVols)
        if gNewDay
            vPV     := 0.0
            vV      := 0.0
            vSCount := 0
            vMCount := 0
            vYCount := 0
        else if not na(vOpen)
            vPV := vPV + (vHigh + vLow + vClose) / 3 * vVol
            vV  := vV + vVol
        vOpen    := open
        vHigh    := high
        vLow     := low
        vVol     := volume
        vSFired  := false
        vMFired  := false
        vYFired  := false
    else
        vHigh := math.max(vHigh, high)
        vLow  := math.min(vLow, low)
        vVol  := vVol + volume
    vClose := close
    float vTPV    = vPV + (vHigh + vLow + close) / 3 * vVol    // today, the forming candle included
    float vTV     = vV + vVol
    float vVw     = vTV > 0 ? vTPV / vTV : na
    float vMw     = not na(vMBV) and vMBV + vTV > 0 ? (vMBPV + vTPV) / (vMBV + vTV) : na
    float vYw     = not na(vYBV) and vYBV + vTV > 0 ? (vYBPV + vTPV) / (vYBV + vTV) : na
    float vAvgVol = array.size(vVols) > 0 ? array.avg(vVols) : na
    float vVolX   = not na(vAvgVol) and vAvgVol > 0 ? vVol / vAvgVol : na
    bool  vOkAll  = vbOk and vInWin and (not vbGainOn or gOk)
    bool  vFireS  = vOkAll and vbSession and vbCan(vVw, vBand, vOpen, vSFired)
    bool  vFireM  = vOkAll and vbMonth and vbCan(vMw, vBand, vOpen, vMFired)
    bool  vFireY  = vOkAll and vbYear and vbCan(vYw, vBand, vOpen, vYFired)
    if vFireS
        vSFired := true
        vSCount := vSCount + 1
    if vFireM
        vMFired := true
        vMCount := vMCount + 1
    if vFireY
        vYFired := true
        vYCount := vYCount + 1
    // v25 BREAK: a bar reaching one tick over the level (when a buy stop there fills), from the
    // bar the level was set on. v25 also cancelled it on any 30s close under the line, which on
    // the candle's chart is only a wick (XXII 10-23, 10m: the level 0.4099 died on a 30s close at
    // 0.3374, the 10m candle closed ~0.40; the break came in the next candle, no alert). Since v26
    // the cancel waits for the candle's close (above).
    if vLvOn and vInWin
        if high >= vLvHigh + syminfo.mintick
            vLvOn     := false
            vBrk      := true
            vBrkCount := vBrkCount + 1
    vPrevVw := vVw
    vPrevMw := vMw
    vPrevYw := vYw
    [vFireS, vFireM, vFireY, vVw, vMw, vYw, vBand, vOpen, gDay, gAh, vVolX, vSCount, vMCount, vYCount, vSet, vBrk, vLvHigh, vLvLow, vLvS, vLvM, vLvY, vBrkCount]

// On the alert's own chart (30s): the alert, and its markers there.
[vbFireS, vbFireM, vbFireY, vbVw, vbMw, vbYw, vbBand, vbOpen, vbDayG, vbAhG, vbVolX, vbNS, vbNM, vbNY, vbSet, vbBrk, vbLvHigh, vbLvLow, vbLvS, vbLvM, vbLvY, vbBrkN] = vbStep()
// On the candle timeframe's chart: the same 30s bars inside each candle.
vbView() =>
    [vwS, vwM, vwY, vwVw, vwMw, vwYw, vwBand, vwOpen, vwDayG, vwAhG, vwVolX, vwNS, vwNM, vwNY, vwSet, vwBrk, vwLvH, vwLvL, vwLvS, vwLvM, vwLvY, vwBrkN] = vbStep()
    [vwS, vwM, vwY, vwBand, vwBrk]
vbBaseSec  = timeframe.in_seconds(vbTf)
vbChartSec = timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period)
vbLower    = vbOk and vbShow and timeframe.period == vbCandleTf and vbChartSec > vbBaseSec
[vbInS, vbInM, vbInY, vbInUp, vbInBrk] = request.security_lower_tf(syminfo.tickerid, vbLower ? vbTf : timeframe.period, vbView())
bool  vbMarkS = false
bool  vbMarkM = false
bool  vbMarkY = false
bool  vbMarkB = false
float vbUp    = na
if vbLower
    int vbIn = array.size(vbInS)
    if vbIn > 0
        vbUp := array.get(vbInUp, vbIn - 1)   // the band at the candle's last 30s close
        for k = 0 to vbIn - 1
            if array.get(vbInS, k)
                vbMarkS := true
            if array.get(vbInM, k)
                vbMarkM := true
            if array.get(vbInY, k)
                vbMarkY := true
            if array.get(vbInBrk, k)
                vbMarkB := true
else if vbOk and vbShow and vbChartSec == vbBaseSec
    vbMarkS := vbFireS
    vbMarkM := vbFireM
    vbMarkY := vbFireY
    vbMarkB := vbBrk
    vbUp    := vbBand

// The message — a contract with services/tv-setups.ts parseTvMessage. The VWAPs are
// the setup's lines (the candle timeframe's session VWAP, the hourly-anchored month
// and year VWAPs), upper the BB timeframe's band, open the candle's:
//   CROSS AIXI 2.61 | sVWAP 2.47 (+5.7%) | mVWAP 2.55 (+2.4%) | yVWAP 3.1 (-15.8%) | upper 2.58 (+1.2%) | open 2.5 | line session+month | candle 5 | bb 2 | cross 1 | day high +25% | vol 1.8x | tf 30S
vbSend = vbOk and timeframe.period == vbTf
vbMsg() =>
    string names = ""
    int    n     = 999
    if vbFireS
        names := pbJoin(names, "session")
        n     := math.min(n, vbNS)
    if vbFireM
        names := pbJoin(names, "month")
        n     := math.min(n, vbNM)
    if vbFireY
        names := pbJoin(names, "year")
        n     := math.min(n, vbNY)
    string msg = "CROSS " + syminfo.ticker + " " + str.tostring(close, format.mintick)
    if not na(vbVw)
        msg += " | sVWAP " + str.tostring(vbVw, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(vbVw) + "%)"
    if not na(vbMw)
        msg += " | mVWAP " + str.tostring(vbMw, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(vbMw) + "%)"
    if not na(vbYw)
        msg += " | yVWAP " + str.tostring(vbYw, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(vbYw) + "%)"
    msg += " | upper " + str.tostring(vbBand, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(vbBand) + "%)"
    msg += " | open " + str.tostring(vbOpen, format.mintick)
    msg += " | line " + names + " | candle " + vbCandleTf + " | bb " + vbBbTf + " | cross " + str.tostring(n)
    if not na(vbDayG)
        msg += " | day high " + (vbDayG >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(vbDayG, "#") + "%"
    if not na(vbAhG)
        msg += " | ah " + (vbAhG >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(vbAhG, "#") + "%"
    if not na(vbVolX)
        msg += " | vol " + str.tostring(vbVolX, "#.#") + "x"
    msg + " | tf " + timeframe.period

if vbSend and (vbFireS or vbFireM or vbFireY)
    alert(vbMsg(), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)

// v25 (operator, 10-22, TANH and SHFS on 10m charts: "the latest VB candle's high should become a
// resistance line and I want to be notified when price crosses over that resistance line (or a
// little bit earlier)"). Measured first (research/vwap-bb-cross, 06-12 → 10-20, session line): a
// buy stop over the VB candle's high beat buying the CROSS by 0.6–0.7 points a trade (still about
// −1% on average, a heads-up), and buying a close above it was ~0.7 points worse than the buy stop;
// the break came a median 3–4 min after the candle closed. So LEVEL goes out when the VB candle
// closes (the "earlier": place the buy stop), and BREAK when a bar reaches one tick over the high.
// A newer VB candle replaces the level; a close under the line the candle crossed cancels it
// (a third fewer, same result), and so does the day's end. No line on the chart (operator).
// v26 (operator, XXII 10-23: "it acts like a resistance"): the close that cancels is a candle's
// close on the VB timeframe, the VB candle's own included, not a 30s close. Measured (10m, 2m band,
// 2R target, 6 candles): 2,755 breaks at −0.08R vs 2,461 at −0.09R with the 30s-style cancel.
//   LEVEL TANH 12.48 | level 12.59 | stop 11.8 | sVWAP 12.1 (+3.1%) | … | line month | candle 10 | bb 2 | tf 30S
//   BREAK TANH 12.6 | level 12.59 | stop 11.8 | … | line month | candle 10 | bb 2 | break 1 | day high +60% | tf 30S
vbLvMsg(string head) =>
    string names = ""
    if vbLvS
        names := pbJoin(names, "session")
    if vbLvM
        names := pbJoin(names, "month")
    if vbLvY
        names := pbJoin(names, "year")
    string msg = head + " " + syminfo.ticker + " " + str.tostring(close, format.mintick)
    msg += " | level " + str.tostring(vbLvHigh, format.mintick) + " | stop " + str.tostring(vbLvLow, format.mintick)
    if not na(vbVw)
        msg += " | sVWAP " + str.tostring(vbVw, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(vbVw) + "%)"
    if not na(vbMw)
        msg += " | mVWAP " + str.tostring(vbMw, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(vbMw) + "%)"
    if not na(vbYw)
        msg += " | yVWAP " + str.tostring(vbYw, format.mintick) + " (" + pctVs(vbYw) + "%)"
    msg += " | line " + names + " | candle " + vbCandleTf + " | bb " + vbBbTf
    if head == "BREAK"
        msg += " | break " + str.tostring(vbBrkN)
    if not na(vbDayG)
        msg += " | day high " + (vbDayG >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(vbDayG, "#") + "%"
    if not na(vbAhG)
        msg += " | ah " + (vbAhG >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(vbAhG, "#") + "%"
    msg + " | tf " + timeframe.period

if vbSend and vbSet
    alert(vbLvMsg("LEVEL"), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
if vbSend and vbBrk
    alert(vbLvMsg("BREAK"), alert.freq_once_per_bar_close)
plot(vbShow and (vbLower or (vbOk and vbChartSec == vbBaseSec)) ? vbUp : na, "BB upper (VWAP + BB cross)", color.new(color.orange, 20))
// v22: the marker says which line crossed (the year's, then the month's, first): teal
// for the session line, yellow "VB M" for the month line, blue "VB Y" for the year line.
plotshape(vbMarkS and not vbMarkM and not vbMarkY, "VWAP + BB cross (session)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.teal, text = "VB", textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)
plotshape(vbMarkM and not vbMarkY, "VWAP + BB cross (month, v22)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.yellow, text = "VB M", textcolor = color.black, size = size.small)
plotshape(vbMarkY, "VWAP + BB cross (year, v22)", shape.labelup, location.belowbar, color.blue, text = "VB Y", textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)
plotshape(vbMarkB, "VB break (v25)", shape.labeldown, location.abovebar, color.teal, text = "BRK", textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)
